# ====================================================
# WAREHOUSE REST API TESTING - CODE_ASSIGNMENT TASKS
# ====================================================
# BASE URL: http://localhost:8080
# Ensure Quarkus dev server is running: ./mvnw.cmd quarkus:dev
# ====================================================

### ============================================
### TASK 1: LOCATION VALIDATION (Implicit Testing)
### ============================================
### Task 1: LocationGateway.resolveByIdentifier() - Seeded Locations
### Valid Locations (case-insensitive):
### ZWOLLE-001, ZWOLLE-002
### AMSTERDAM-001, AMSTERDAM-002  
### TILBURG-001, HELMOND-001
### EINDHOVEN-001, VETSBY-001
###
### Status Codes:
### 201 Created - Location is valid
### 400 Bad Request - Invalid location
### ============================================

### TEST 1.1: Create Warehouse with VALID location
### EXPECTED: 200 OK
### Location used: AMSTERDAM-002 (max 3 warehouses, capacity 75)
POST http://localhost:8080/warehouse
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "businessUnitCode": "WH-VALID-LOC",
  "location": "AMSTERDAM-002",
  "capacity": 50,
  "stock": 10
}

### TEST 1.2: Create Warehouse with INVALID location
### EXPECTED: 400 Bad Request
### Location "HYDERABAD" does not exist in LocationGateway
POST http://localhost:8080/warehouse
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "businessUnitCode": "WH-INVALID-LOC",
  "location": "HYDERABAD",
  "capacity": 50,
  "stock": 10
}

### TEST 1.3: Create Warehouse with NULL location
### EXPECTED: 400 Bad Request
POST http://localhost:8080/warehouse
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "businessUnitCode": "WH-NULL-LOC",
  "location": null,
  "capacity": 50,
  "stock": 10
}


### ============================================
### TASK 2: STORE (Transaction-Safe Legacy Sync)
### ============================================
### Test Store CRUD operations
### The StoreResource.performLegacyAction() method ensures
### LegacyStoreManagerGateway is called ONLY after DB commit
### Uses: TransactionSynchronizationRegistry + Status.STATUS_COMMITTED
### 
### Pre-existing Stores in DB (from import.sql):
### ID 1: TONSTAD, quantity 10
### ID 2: KALLAX, quantity 5  
### ID 3: BESTÅ, quantity 3
### ============================================

### TEST 2.1: LIST all Stores
### EXPECTED: 200 OK
### Returns: [TONSTAD, KALLAX, BESTÅ, ...]
GET http://localhost:8080/store
Accept: application/json

### TEST 2.2: GET specific Store (ID=1)
### EXPECTED: 200 OK
### Returns: Store with id 1 (TONSTAD)
GET http://localhost:8080/store/1
Accept: application/json

### TEST 2.3: CREATE new Store (Legacy Sync happens AFTER commit)
### EXPECTED: 201 Created
### Response: Store object with generated ID
### NOTE: Legacy system sync happens after DB transaction commits
POST http://localhost:8080/store
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "NEW-STORE",
  "quantityProductsInStock": 20
}

### TEST 2.4: UPDATE Store by ID (Legacy Sync happens AFTER commit)
### EXPECTED: 200 OK
### Store name changed to "UPDATED-TONSTAD"
### NOTE: Legacy sync guarantees DB update before legacy call
PUT http://localhost:8080/store/1
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "UPDATED-TONSTAD",
  "quantityProductsInStock": 15
}

### TEST 2.5: PATCH Store by ID (Partial Update)
### EXPECTED: 200 OK
### Only updates the name field
PATCH http://localhost:8080/store/2
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "PATCHED-KALLAX"
}

### TEST 2.6: UPDATE non-existent Store
### EXPECTED: 404 Not Found
PUT http://localhost:8080/store/9999
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "GHOST-STORE",
  "quantityProductsInStock": 50
}

### TEST 2.7: DELETE Store by ID
### EXPECTED: 204 No Content
DELETE http://localhost:8080/store/3


### ============================================
### TASK 3: WAREHOUSE CRUD Operations
### ============================================
### Three sub-tasks:
### 3a. CREATE: Business Unit uniqueness, Location valid, 
###     Max warehouses per location, Capacity ≤ location.maxCapacity,
###     Stock ≤ capacity, Sets createdAt timestamp
### 3b. REPLACE: Warehouse exists, New capacity ≥ old stock,
###     Stock matches old warehouse
### 3c. ARCHIVE: Soft-delete with archivedAt timestamp
###
### Available Locations for testing:
### ZWOLLE-001 (max 1, capacity 40)
### ZWOLLE-002 (max 2, capacity 50)
### AMSTERDAM-001 (max 5, capacity 100)
### AMSTERDAM-002 (max 3, capacity 75)
### TILBURG-001 (max 1, capacity 40)
### HELMOND-001 (max 1, capacity 45)
### EINDHOVEN-001 (max 2, capacity 70)
### VETSBY-001 (max 1, capacity 90)
### ============================================

### ---- TASK 3a: CREATE Warehouse Tests ----

### TEST 3a.1: CREATE Warehouse - SUCCESS
### EXPECTED: 200 OK
### Creates WH-CREATE-001 at AMSTERDAM-002
POST http://localhost:8080/warehouse
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "businessUnitCode": "WH-CREATE-001",
  "location": "AMSTERDAM-002",
  "capacity": 50,
  "stock": 10
}

### TEST 3a.2: CREATE Warehouse - DUPLICATE Business Unit Code
### EXPECTED: 409 Conflict
### Business Unit Code already exists (from TEST 3a.1)
POST http://localhost:8080/warehouse
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "businessUnitCode": "WH-CREATE-001",
  "location": "ZWOLLE-002",
  "capacity": 40,
  "stock": 5
}

### TEST 3a.3: CREATE Warehouse - INVALID Location
### EXPECTED: 400 Bad Request
### Location "INVALID-CITY" doesn't exist
POST http://localhost:8080/warehouse
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "businessUnitCode": "WH-CREATE-002",
  "location": "INVALID-CITY",
  "capacity": 50,
  "stock": 10
}

### TEST 3a.4: CREATE Warehouse - Capacity exceeds location.maxCapacity
### EXPECTED: 400 Bad Request
### AMSTERDAM-002 has maxCapacity 75, trying 80
POST http://localhost:8080/warehouse
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "businessUnitCode": "WH-CREATE-003",
  "location": "AMSTERDAM-002",
  "capacity": 80,
  "stock": 10
}

### TEST 3a.5: CREATE Warehouse - Stock exceeds capacity
### EXPECTED: 400 Bad Request
### Stock 60 > Capacity 50
POST http://localhost:8080/warehouse
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "businessUnitCode": "WH-CREATE-004",
  "location": "AMSTERDAM-002",
  "capacity": 50,
  "stock": 60
}

### TEST 3a.6: CREATE Warehouse - Exceeds max warehouses at location
### EXPECTED: 400 Bad Request
### TILBURG-001 allows max 1 warehouse (already has 1)
POST http://localhost:8080/warehouse
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "businessUnitCode": "WH-CREATE-005",
  "location": "TILBURG-001",
  "capacity": 40,
  "stock": 5
}

### TEST 3a.7: CREATE Warehouse - All validations pass
### EXPECTED: 200 OK
### Valid location, BU code, capacity, stock
POST http://localhost:8080/warehouse
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "businessUnitCode": "WH-ALL-VALID",
  "location": "EINDHOVEN-001",
  "capacity": 60,
  "stock": 20
}

### ---- TASK 3b: RETRIEVE Warehouse Tests ----

### TEST 3b.1: LIST all Warehouses
### EXPECTED: 200 OK
### Returns list of all non-archived warehouses
GET http://localhost:8080/warehouse
Accept: application/json

### TEST 3b.2: GET Warehouse by Business Unit Code
### EXPECTED: 200 OK
### Returns WH-CREATE-001
GET http://localhost:8080/warehouse/WH-CREATE-001
Accept: application/json

### TEST 3b.3: GET non-existent Warehouse
### EXPECTED: 404 Not Found
GET http://localhost:8080/warehouse/WH-DOES-NOT-EXIST
Accept: application/json

### ---- TASK 3c: REPLACE Warehouse Tests ----

### TEST 3c.1: REPLACE Warehouse - SUCCESS
### EXPECTED: 200 OK
### Increase capacity from 50 to 70 (stock stays same 10)
POST http://localhost:8080/warehouse/WH-CREATE-001/replacement
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "businessUnitCode": "WH-CREATE-001",
  "location": "AMSTERDAM-002",
  "capacity": 70,
  "stock": 10
}

### TEST 3c.2: REPLACE Warehouse - Non-existent warehouse
### EXPECTED: 404 Not Found
POST http://localhost:8080/warehouse/WH-NOT-FOUND/replacement
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "businessUnitCode": "WH-NOT-FOUND",
  "location": "AMSTERDAM-002",
  "capacity": 50,
  "stock": 10
}

### TEST 3c.3: REPLACE Warehouse - New capacity < old stock
### EXPECTED: 400 Bad Request
### Old warehouse has stock 20, trying capacity 10 (too small)
POST http://localhost:8080/warehouse/WH-ALL-VALID/replacement
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "businessUnitCode": "WH-ALL-VALID",
  "location": "EINDHOVEN-001",
  "capacity": 10,
  "stock": 20
}

### TEST 3c.4: REPLACE Warehouse - Stock doesn't match
### EXPECTED: 400 Bad Request
### Old warehouse has stock 20, trying new stock 25 (mismatch)
POST http://localhost:8080/warehouse/WH-ALL-VALID/replacement
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "businessUnitCode": "WH-ALL-VALID",
  "location": "EINDHOVEN-001",
  "capacity": 70,
  "stock": 25
}

### ---- TASK 3d: ARCHIVE Warehouse Tests ----

### TEST 3d.1: ARCHIVE Warehouse - SUCCESS
### EXPECTED: 204 No Content
### Sets archivedAt timestamp, warehouse won't appear in LIST
DELETE http://localhost:8080/warehouse/WH-CREATE-001

### TEST 3d.2: LIST Warehouses after ARCHIVE
### EXPECTED: 200 OK
### WH-CREATE-001 should NOT appear (archived)
GET http://localhost:8080/warehouse
Accept: application/json

### TEST 3d.3: GET archived Warehouse (by ID)
### EXPECTED: Should NOT be found (filtered in repository)
GET http://localhost:8080/warehouse/WH-CREATE-001
Accept: application/json

### TEST 3d.4: ARCHIVE non-existent Warehouse
### EXPECTED: 404 Not Found
DELETE http://localhost:8080/warehouse/WH-ARCHIVE-NOT-FOUND


### ============================================
### REFERENCE: HTTP Status Codes Used
### ============================================
### 200 OK              - Request successful, resource returned
### 201 Created         - Resource created successfully
### 204 No Content      - Request successful, no content returned
### 400 Bad Request     - Validation error (invalid data)
### 404 Not Found       - Resource doesn't exist
### 409 Conflict        - Business Unit Code already exists
### 422 Unprocessable   - Invalid request format
### 500 Server Error    - Internal error
### ============================================

### Notes:
### - Each request can be executed by clicking "Send Request" in VS Code
### - Responses appear in the side panel
### - Use ### to separate tests and add comments
### - Modify values as needed for testing
